why Opens Ravenholdt Manor, the hidden rogue house in the Alterac hills, and Myrokos's jobs against the Syndicate.

# Ravenholdt for Rogues of both factions: The Manor, Ravenholdt (6681, from
# the Elegant Letter at 24) to Fahrad, then Forever's new jobs for Myrokos
# Silentform at the manor (Forever's quest data; Ravenholdt reputation and
# money, no items):
# - Syndicate Sabotage (96779, level 24): Lord Tomas in Durnholde Keep. 100 rep.
# - What's the Big Idea? (96781, level 36) and Covert Extraction (96782, its
#   follow-up): Barton's report at Strahnbrad, then the Perenolde heirlooms in
#   two towers of the Ruins of Alterac. 100 rep each; 40s for 96782.
# - A Way In (96783), Master of Disguise (96784), Ain't No Telling (96785) and
#   The Syndicate Sting (96786), level 34-36: a uniform from Northfold Manor,
#   Anastasia Miller in Stromgarde, her stash, the handoff at Thoradin's Wall.
#   35s, 35s and 70s with 300 rep.
# - Syndicate Emblems (6701): the Ravenholdt Guards' repeatable reputation
#   turn-in, 100 rep each (Ravenholdt reputation must be Neutral or better).
# Sources: Forever's Rogue class quest list (data/local/quest-audit/) and
# Forever's quest pages (page snapshot) for the quests, texts, reputation and
# money; quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the givers,
# places and the Elegant Letter's givers (every capital's rogue trainer);
# the KB for the starts quests.json lacks (Myrokos gives 96782; Anastasia
# Miller 96785 and 96786); npcs.json for the Syndicate levels (Durnholde 20-21,
# Northfold Manor 30-32, Stromgarde's Prowlers and Conjurors 35-36 elite) and
# Lord Tomas's 15 spawn points; data/local/mechanics (quest-steps and
# quest-notes, checked 2026-10-20) for the Rite of Cunning (Detect Traps at
# the tunnel chest, Milton if it is opened), Barton's pickpocket-only report,
# and the places our data has no spawn for: the two heirloom towers, the
# Syndicate Footlocker at Northfold Manor, Anastasia Miller on her ledge, her
# stash and the shipment at the south end of Thoradin's Wall (players' notes;
# their map frame is not recorded).
# Races: quests.json and the KB give every Syndicate quest to both sides
# except Master of Disguise (96784, Horde races only). Forever's quest page
# files Covert Extraction (96782) as Alliance, but that is not a lock: the
# Forever dialog captures have an Orc rogue taking and handing in Covert
# Extraction at Myrokos (and What's the Big Idea?, A Way In, Master of
# Disguise and Ain't No Telling), and the server's quest answers in players'
# caches (EG Link, client 1.60.1.70450) set no race limit on any of 96781-96786.
# Ain't No Telling (96785) has no prerequisite in our data, so Alliance
# rogues go from the footlocker straight to Anastasia.
# INGAME: does the Syndicate Footlocker offer Master of Disguise (96784) to an Alliance rogue too? (Horde: yes, dialog captures; server: no race limit; quests.json: Horde only.)
# Players' caches (EG Link): both Master of Disguise (96784) and Ain't No
# Telling (96785) hand out the Syndicate Uniform (275706) when accepted, so a
# rogue who cannot take 96784 still gets it from Anastasia.
# Junkboxes Needed (8249, level 50+ repeatable, Fahrad) is left out: its
# Heavy Junkboxes come from level 50+ pickpocketing.
# Based on data, not play past 30: the jobs above 30 are above the beta's
# level cap until launch on 4 November.

step The Elegant Letter
  tip At 24 any capital's rogue trainer (Master Mathias Shaw or Osborne the Night Man in Stormwind, Gest or Ormok in Orgrimmar, and the others) has an Elegant Letter from Ravenholdt for you: ask for it in their talk window. Open it: the quest gives you the Seal of Ravenholdt for Fahrad. Learn Detect Traps from your trainer first if you have not; the way in is a test of it.
  level 24
  accept 6681 item 17126                      -- Elegant Letter

step Ravenholdt Manor
  tip Horde fly to Tarren Mill, Alliance to Southshore. The trail to the manor is hard to see: it starts behind the plateau north of Durnholde Keep, east of Tarren Mill, climbs into the hills and bends twice to a small tunnel. A chest sits in the tunnel: do not open it. Cast Detect Traps near it and walk up close; that is the Rite of Cunning (it comes back after 5 minutes). Opening the chest calls Milton, an elite rogue of about level 32. Through the tunnel lies Ravenholdt Manor: Fahrad is upstairs inside. Do not attack anyone at the manor: it costs Ravenholdt reputation.
  kill 13936 quest 6681.1                     -- Rite of Cunning: Detect Traps beside the tunnel chest
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 6681                                 -- Fahrad
  accept 96779                                -- Myrokos Silentform
  accept 6701 optional                        -- Ravenholdt Guard: Syndicate Emblems, repeatable; take it now, the emblems are quest items

step Lord Tomas
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Lord Tomas is inside Durnholde Keep, the Syndicate fortress south of the manor; he can stand in any of fifteen spots in the keep, so search. Quick and quiet, says Myrokos. Pick the pockets of the level 20-21 Syndicate Rogues, Shadow Mages and Watchmen on your way: they carry Syndicate Emblems for the guards' repeatable reputation quest.
  kill 266216 quest 96779.1                   -- Lord Tomas
  collect 17124 quest 6701.1 optional "Pick Pocket Syndicate members for Syndicate Emblems"

step Myrokos Silentform
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 96779                                -- Myrokos Silentform
  turnin 6701 optional                        -- Ravenholdt Guard: one emblem each time, 100 reputation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Myrokos's mid-30s jobs

step What's the Big Idea?
  tip In your mid 30s Myrokos has two more jobs; take both. Barton leads a Syndicate scouting party at Strahnbrad, in the east of the Alterac Mountains, inside one of the houses with stealthed Syndicate around him. Pick his pocket for the report and do not kill him: he does not drop it. If you are lower than him he sees through stealth; Master of Deception helps, or Distract him, Vanish and come in from behind. Pick Pocket can miss several times in a row.
  level 34
  accept 96781                                -- Myrokos Silentform
  accept 96783
  collect 275482 quest 96781.1 @62.6,46.9 "Pick Pocket Barton for Barton's Scouting Report"

step Covert Extraction
  tip Back to Myrokos; the report sends you after the Perenolde heirlooms. Two towers stand among the Ruins of Alterac, in the middle of the Alterac Mountains, held by ogres: the shield lies in the northern tower, the sword in the southern one, which elite ogres ring and watch from far off. Stay stealthed; nothing guards the heirlooms inside.
  turnin 96781                                -- Myrokos Silentform
  accept 96782 npc 13085
  collect 275636 quest 96782.2 @41.35,40.16   -- Royal Aegis of Perenolde, in the northern tower
  collect 275635 quest 96782.1 @38.5,58.0     -- Blade of House Perenolde, in the southern tower
  turnin 96782                                -- Myrokos Silentform

step A Way In
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Stromgarde Keep in western Arathi is a Syndicate stronghold; to get in you need a uniform. Northfold Manor, in north-western Arathi, is held by Syndicate Highwaymen, Pathstalkers and Mercenaries (level 30-32): find the Syndicate Footlocker there and take the uniform; that ends A Way In.
  turnin 96783 object 656157 @32.3,26.6       -- Syndicate Footlocker, Northfold Manor
  accept 96784 object 656157 @32.3,26.6 only Horde -- Master of Disguise: the Syndicate Uniform

step Anastasia Miller
  tip Stromgarde's Syndicate Prowlers and Conjurors are elite (level 35-36): a rogue of 36 can slip past them, but fighting one alone is hard, so stay hidden or bring a friend. Put on the Syndicate Uniform (Master of Disguise hands it to you at the footlocker) to pass as one of them; stealth or suspicious acts can break it. If the footlocker gave you no uniform, Anastasia hands you one with Ain't No Telling. Anastasia Miller is not inside the keep: she stands on a ledge on the outside of the castle wall. Jump across to it from the roof of the house beside the ledge.
  turnin 96784 @26.8,64.4 only Horde          -- Anastasia Miller
  accept 96785 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4          -- Ain't No Telling

step Ain't No Telling
  tip She will not talk without something to bargain with. Her stash is upstairs in a house close to the keep: take the Stolen Funds. If it is already open, wait for it to come back.
  collect 275709 quest 96785.1 @29.5,65.1     -- Stolen Funds: Anastasia's Stash
  turnin 96785 @26.8,64.4                     -- Anastasia Miller
  accept 96786 npc 266847 @26.8,64.4          -- The Syndicate Sting

step The Syndicate Sting
  tip Falconcrest's men make the handoff at the southern end of Thoradin's Wall, the old wall between Arathi and Hillsbrad. Kill the two guarding the box and take the Intercepted Shipment. Keep the Syndicate Uniform: Myrokos wants it back with the shipment.
  collect 275882 quest 96786.1 @15.5,43.0     -- Intercepted Shipment

step Back to Myrokos
  zone Alterac Mountains
  turnin 96786                                -- Myrokos Silentform: 70 silver, 300 Ravenholdt reputation
